{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>וּתְקַעְתֶּם תְּרוּעָה שֵׁנִית</b>. And a single blast was not sufficient for all of them, in the manner that one blows a single blast for west and north together, as they say in Sifrei (25:73). The reason is that they would take down the Mishkan and the children of Gershon would set out before the standard of the children of Reuben would move southward; therefore a separate blast is needed after the Mishkan's departure."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:07:11.101604558Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}